<Layouts.public_nav current_scope={@current_scope} flash={@flash} />

<div class="pt-28 pb-24 px-6 bg-canvas min-h-screen">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-10">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <div class="[&_h2]:text-base [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_p]:text-sm [&_p]:text-steel [&_p]:leading-relaxed [&_p]:mb-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ul]:space-y-1.5 [&_ul]:text-sm [&_ul]:text-steel [&_ul]:mb-3 [&_a]:text-mint [&_a]:hover:underline [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-ink">
      <h2>1. What We Collect</h2>
      <p>We collect the following information when you use Speechwave:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> — used to create and manage your account.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage data</strong>
          — number of sessions, participants, and reactions, used to provide analytics, enforce plan limits, and improve the service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Chrome extension data</strong>
          — if you use the Speechwave Chrome extension, your Speechwave API key is stored locally in your browser, not on our servers. While a session is active, the extension also sends the current Google Slides slide number to our server so reactions can be attributed to the right slide.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Audience members who use the reaction page are anonymous. We do not
        collect any personal information from audience members. To count how
        many people reacted, the reaction page creates a random identifier
        and keeps it in your browser's local storage for that talk. It
        contains nothing about you or your device and is not shared between
        talks. Our server stores only a one-way hash of it combined with the
        session, so reactions cannot be linked across sessions. You can clear
        the identifier at any time by clearing your browser's site data.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email address to send login links (we use passwordless,
        magic-link authentication) and to confirm changes when you update your
        account email. We use usage data solely to provide and improve the
        Service, including enforcing free tier limits.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data Storage</h2>
      <p>
        Your data is stored on infrastructure provided by <a href="https://fly.io" target="_blank">Fly.io</a>,
        located in the United States. Your Speechwave API key, when used with
        the Chrome extension, is cached locally in your browser's storage
        instead, so you stay connected between sessions.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep backups of our database so we can recover from failures. Data you
        delete is removed from those backups within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties,
        except as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies and Sessions</h2>
      <p>
        We use a session cookie to keep you logged in. No third-party tracking
        cookies are used.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account yourself from the Settings page. Deleting it
        removes your account and all associated data, including your talks,
        sessions, reactions and settings, immediately. Deleted data is removed
        from our backups within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop a deleted account from being restored from a backup during that
        30 day window, we keep an anonymous account identifier. It is a number
        and the date of the deletion, with no email address or other personal
        details. After 30 days only the date of the deletion remains, with no
        identifier.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you cannot sign in, you can ask us to delete your account by emailing
        us at <a href="mailto:admin@speechwave.live">admin@speechwave.live</a>.
        We will process your request within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Continued use of the Service
        after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, contact us at <a href="mailto:admin@speechwave.live">admin@speechwave.live</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<Layouts.public_footer />
